--- body ---
## Context

`skill-doctor` mined recurring failure patterns out of the harness's own
automation and proposed hardening tickets, never applying them. Good design,
and it is not being removed for going unused — it is being removed because
ticket 0882 deleted its evidence.

Six of its seven clusterers read the nightbeat supervisor's journal or the
nightbeat run logs: budget raises, dirty trees blocking a checkout, watermark
redetection, unclosed umbrella tickets, max-turns exhaustion, crash recovery.
Nothing writes either source any more. 0882 removed those six rather than
leave them reporting "no pattern" forever.

The seventh reads git history, and it is not blind: over a 180-day window it
has **645 commits** to examine — 4 matching `repair:` and 641 matching
`ticket(` — and reports zero. That is an honest negative, not a broken probe.
The defect it detects, an inconsistent `Ticket:` line format, was fixed long
ago and has not recurred.

Usage matches: 3 invocations in the measured window, the last on 2026-06-23.

## What survives the removal, deliberately

The five-way root-cause taxonomy (Agent Error, Extractor Error, Original
Error, Missing Data, Other) was a convention **shared** between this skill and
`verify-gate`. `verify-gate` is live — 56 invocations across 14 projects — so
the vocabulary keeps a holder. `tests/test_root_cause_taxonomy.py` narrows to
that holder rather than being deleted: a taxonomy that silently loses a
category is still a real defect, and one file is enough to guard it. What the
test can no longer prove is cross-file agreement, and its docstring must say
so instead of implying a check it no longer performs.

## The alternative, considered and declined

The harness gained a durable evidence base this morning: `scripts/census/`
reads session traces, which exist for every session whether or not a night
pipeline runs. Repointing `skill-doctor` at them would give it a corpus again.
That is rebuilding, not repairing — second-order work of exactly the kind the
2026-07-14 cool-down targets, proposed on a day spent removing surface. If the
self-diagnosis loop is wanted back, it is a design decision to take
deliberately, on the traces, not a debt to carry meanwhile.

## Observed while doing this, not acted on

`trace-doctor` looked like the same case and is not. Its evidence base is the
session traces, which exist for every session and are alive; the micro-turn
rule in `workflow.md` names it for future re-measures, so removing it would
leave a rule pointing at nothing. Its whole family ran over five days in
mid-July (`trace_ab_harvest` 17 runs, `trace-stats` 15, down to `trace-digest`
at zero) with one return on 2026-08-14 — under-used, not dead.

What it does raise is a duplication this pass created: `scripts/trace-*.py`
and `scripts/census/` now read the same corpus. Which absorbs which is a
design question, filed here as an observation.

## Relevant files

- `skills/skill-doctor/` — 3 645 B
- `scripts/skill-doctor-survey.py` — 13 414 B, one clusterer left of seven
- `tests/test_skill_doctor_survey.py` — 10 tests left of 44
- `tests/test_root_cause_taxonomy.py` — narrows to verify-gate
- `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md` — one passing mention
- `README.md` — generated catalog

## Test

`tests/test_root_cause_taxonomy.py` is the red step: three of its five
assertions read `skills/skill-doctor/SKILL.md` — two directly, and the
cross-file token check through both holders — and fail the moment it is gone.
Run the suite before editing it, so the failures name the couplings rather
than a manifest guessing them (the lesson 0882 paid for).

## Verification

- [x] The suite went red on `test_root_cause_taxonomy.py` before that file was
      edited — three failures, exactly the three predicted
- [x] The narrowed guard passes, and gained a corpus check of its own: every
      assertion now reads a single file, so that file's absence would turn the
      rest green over nothing
- [x] No reference to `skill-doctor` survives outside `docs/`, `tickets/` and the
      one line of the guard that records why it lost a holder
- [x] `make check-skills-drift` passes after `make skills-catalog`
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- `verify-gate` keeps its taxonomy, its field and its guard.
- No other skill changes behaviour.

## Exit criteria

- The skill, its survey and its tests are gone; the shared vocabulary keeps
  its live holder and its guard.
